        // Actually, updateMaxNodeDelegatorCount is onlyLRTAdmin, and after initialization the admin is the zero address role?
        // DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE = 0x00, and it is checked on the lrtConfig which we pass.
        // We cannot guarantee that lrtConfig address has the admin role.
        // So we take a different approach: we fuzz lrtConfig address such that it can act as admin.
        // But we are restricted from vm.mockCall.
        // Alternative: we can test the property that after initialization succeeds, any subsequent initialize call reverts.
        // The bug allows re-initialization which *can* change maxNodeDelegatorCount if a different config is passed
        // that resets it to 10. But our property is that it must revert, so we don't need to change maxNodeDelegatorCount beforehand.
        // The bug breaks because re-initialization with a new config resets maxNodeDelegatorCount to 10,
        // but our assertion is just that the second call must revert. So we don't need to fiddle with maxNodeDelegatorCount at all.

        // Second initialization attempt
        bool secondInitReverted = false;
        try c.initialize(newLrtConfig) {
            secondInitReverted = false;
        } catch {
            secondInitReverted = true;
        }

        assertTrue(secondInitReverted);
    }
}

